# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Setup {#setup}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Begin by importing the necessary libraries and defining the helper functions that build the quantum circuits for the LSH time evolution. There are three core circuit-building functions:\n"
msgstr "Simulan sa pag-import ng mga kailangang library at pagdedefine ng mga helper function na bumubuo ng quantum circuits para sa LSH time evolution. May tatlong core circuit-building function:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`pair_hamiltonian_circuit`**: Implements the two-qubit unitary $U_I$ for the approximate interaction Hamiltonian between neighboring sites. The gate decomposition is: $\\text{CNOT} \\to H \\to R_z(-c) \\to \\text{CNOT} \\to R_z(c) \\to \\text{CNOT} \\to H \\to \\text{CNOT}$.\n"
msgstr "**`pair_hamiltonian_circuit`**: Ipinapatupad ang two-qubit unitary $U_I$ para sa approximate interaction Hamiltonian sa pagitan ng mga karatig na site. Ang gate decomposition ay: $\\text{CNOT} \\to H \\to R_z(-c) \\to \\text{CNOT} \\to R_z(c) \\to \\text{CNOT} \\to H \\to \\text{CNOT}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`electric_hamiltonian_circuit`**: Implements the two-qubit unitary $U_E$ for the approximate electric field energy at each site. The gate decomposition is: $X \\to R_z(\\theta/2) \\to \\text{CNOT} \\to R_z(-\\theta/2) \\to \\text{CNOT} \\to R_z(\\theta/2) \\to X$.\n"
msgstr "**`electric_hamiltonian_circuit`**: Ipinapatupad ang two-qubit unitary $U_E$ para sa approximate electric field energy sa bawat site. Ang gate decomposition ay: $X \\to R_z(\\theta/2) \\to \\text{CNOT} \\to R_z(-\\theta/2) \\to \\text{CNOT} \\to R_z(\\theta/2) \\to X$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`construct_circuit`**: Assembles the full Trotterized circuit, layering interaction, electric, and mass terms with SWAP gates to manage qubit connectivity.\n"
msgstr "**`construct_circuit`**: Isinasama ang buong Trotterized circuit, sa pamamagitan ng pag-layer ng interaction, electric, at mass terms na may SWAP gates upang pamahalaan ang qubit connectivity.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, demonstrate the workflow at small scale using a six-site lattice (12 qubits), so that you can verify circuit construction and understand the physical observables before running on hardware.\n"
msgstr "Una, ipakita ang workflow sa maliit na sukat gamit ang isang six-site lattice (12 qubits), upang ma-verify mo ang circuit construction at maintindihan ang physical observables bago patakbuhin sa hardware.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the physical parameters matching the weak-coupling regime studied in the paper ($x = 100$, $m/g = 1$). The derived circuit parameters are:\n"
msgstr "Idepine ang mga physical parameter na tumutugma sa weak-coupling regime na pinag-aralan sa papel ($x = 100$, $m/g = 1$). Ang mga derived circuit parameter ay:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$c = \\delta_\\tau \\cdot x = 0.15$ (interaction parameter)\n"
msgstr "$c = \\delta_\\tau \\cdot x = 0.15$ (interaction parameter)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\theta = -\\delta_\\tau (\\bar{n}_l/2 + 3/4) = 0.01$ (electric field phase)\n"
msgstr "$\\theta = -\\delta_\\tau (\\bar{n}_l/2 + 3/4) = 0.01$ (electric field phase)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\tilde{m} = \\delta_\\tau \\cdot \\mu = 0.03$ (mass parameter)\n"
msgstr "$\\tilde{m} = \\delta_\\tau \\cdot \\mu = 0.03$ (mass parameter)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each Trotter step count, build **two circuits**: one initializing a meson at the center (`inverse_mid=True`) and one preparing the strong-coupling vacuum (`inverse_mid=False`). The differential measurement protocol subtracts the vacuum evolution to isolate the hadron signal.\n"
msgstr "Para sa bawat bilang ng Trotter step, bumuo ng **dalawang circuit**: isang nag-iinitialize ng meson sa gitna (`inverse_mid=True`) at isa na naghahanda ng strong-coupling vacuum (`inverse_mid=False`). Ang differential measurement protocol ay ibinabawas ang vacuum evolution upang ihiwalay ang hadron signal.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/loop-string-hadron-dynamics/extracted-outputs/step1-circuits-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/loop-string-hadron-dynamics/extracted-outputs/step1-circuits-1.avif)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the observables: single-qubit $Z$ measurements on every qubit. From $\\langle Z \\rangle$ you can extract occupation probabilities and then the staggered fermion number $n_f(r)$ at each lattice site $r$.\n"
msgstr "Idepine ang mga observable: single-qubit $Z$ measurements sa bawat qubit. Mula sa $\\langle Z \\rangle$ maaari mong i-extract ang occupation probabilities at pagkatapos ang staggered fermion number $n_f(r)$ sa bawat lattice site $r$.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use `StatevectorEstimator` for exact noiseless simulation at small scale.\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang `StatevectorEstimator` para sa exact noiseless simulation sa maliit na sukat.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
